# qwen3-uncensored — Qwen3 14B Uncensored Q4_K_M at a 32K window. Wants a 12GB+ card.
#
# Pairs with:
#     model pull … --engine llama --kind model --name qwen3-14b-uncensored-q4_k_m
#
# 🔴 The model and this file travel together. Applying this profile without the
# 14B weights on disk leaves the engine pointing at a directory that is not
# there; pulling the weights without applying this profile leaves 8.4GB unused
# while the old model keeps serving.
PROFILE_NAME=qwen3-uncensored
PROFILE_APPLIED_AT=
IMAGE_NAME=ghcr.io/isannai/llama
IMAGE_TAG=latest
CONTAINER_NAME=llama
PORT=7862
IP=10.10.1.13
MODELS_DIR=./.temp/models/defaults
# Lowercase, because the store directory is. /models inside the container is
# case-sensitive even when the host filesystem is not, so a case-shifted path
# loads on Windows and fails on Linux.
MODEL=qwen3-14b-uncensored-q4_k_m/qwen3-14b-uncensored-q4_k_m.gguf
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=qwen3-14b-uncensored
# 32768 against a 40960 trained window — under the model's ceiling, not at it.
# It only fits because KV_TYPE quantizes the cache: at f16 a 32K cache is ~5.4GB
# and will not sit beside 8.4GB of weights on a 12GB card. If the card is also
# driving a desktop and generation slows, CTX_SIZE=24576 is the first cut —
# Windows spills to host memory instead of refusing, so the symptom is slowness
# rather than an out-of-memory error.
CTX_SIZE=32768
GPU_LAYERS=99
SPLIT_MODE=
PARALLEL=1
SLOTS=
THREADS=
# q8_0 puts the 32K cache at ~2.7GB, which loads with a few hundred MB to spare.
# Quantizing the V cache makes llama.cpp require flash attention, so run.sh adds
# --flash-attn on whenever KV_TYPE is not f16. Without it the V cache is read
# wrong and the model emits noise rather than failing — the worse outcome.
KV_TYPE=q8_0
# --jinja, which also hands the model its own chat template. For Qwen3 that
# means thinking mode is on: replies carry <think> blocks.
TOOL_CALLS=on
CHAT_TEMPLATE=
NO_MMAP=
MLOCK=
LORA_DIR=./.temp/models/loras
LORA_ADAPTERS=
# A profile does not normally reach into sampling. This one has to, because
# llama.cpp ships every repetition brake OFF — repeat-penalty 1.00, presence,
# frequency and dry all 0.00, each labelled "= disabled" by its own --help — and
# nothing downstream fills them in: run.sh assembles only infrastructure flags,
# and isann infer sends no sampling fields unless asked. A 14B at Q4_K_M with no
# brake loops. Measured here before this line existed: whole sentences came back
# repeated word for word until the token budget ran out.
#
# presence-penalty alone did not close it — 30-character verbatim spans still
# appeared across 3 runs. dry-multiplier is the sampler built for repeated
# SEQUENCES, and that did: every run capped at 10 characters, which is ordinary
# Korean ending overlap rather than degeneration.
#
# top-k 20 and min-p 0 are what Qwen3 asks for in both thinking and non-thinking
# mode. temp 0.6 / top-p 0.95 are the thinking-mode pair, which is the mode
# --jinja leaves on; non-thinking wants 0.7 / 0.8, so override per request if you
# drive the model with /no_think. These are defaults — any request body wins.
#
# 🔴 The quotes are load-bearing. run.sh sources this file as shell, so an
# unquoted value containing spaces assigns the first word and then tries to RUN
# the second as a command — the container exits 127 before llama-server starts.
# Samplers run over the logit vector, so none of this costs VRAM.
EXTRA_LLAMA_ARGS="--presence-penalty 1.5 --dry-multiplier 0.8 --top-k 20 --min-p 0 --temp 0.6 --top-p 0.95"
